      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1863 Dallas became the oldest incorporated town in Gaston County, serving as the county seat from 1846 to 1911.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dallas%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Gaston County Museum of Art and History, housed in the 1852 Hoffman Hotel, displays the state’s largest collection of horse‑drawn vehicles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dallasnc.net/page/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dallas’s decline began when 1872 commissioners refused to fund bridges for the Atlanta‑Richmond Railway, fearing noisy trains would disturb livestock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dallas%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town celebrated its 150th anniversary in 2015 by restoring the historic courthouse and downtown square, preserving its postcard‑like charm.",
